# Known equivalent changes, kept out on purpose (each guard is also made by something else, so removing it alone changes nothing a caller can see):
#   * pro_booking_state-less 'p.kind = business' in market_is_provider: a personal profile has no category, so the category test already turns it away;
#   * the preference for an accepted quote in pro_request_json: only one quote can be sent or accepted at a time (a sent one is withdrawn when a request is accepted... and an accepted
#     request takes no new quote), so there is never a choice to make;
#   * `on conflict do nothing` in market_payout_make and the zero guard: the callers pass a positive amount once per booking (a booking is cancelled or completed once);
#   * the early return in market_cancel and market_complete: every caller has just looked at the status;
#   * the policy given for a booking that lapsed before any payment (nothing was paid, so nothing is kept whichever policy);
#   * `provider_done_at is not null` in the housekeeping's completion: a null time never compares as old enough.
#   * the amount of a payment that is "full" in pro_payment_begin: a deposit equal to the total is what makes a payment full, so the two amounts are the same number.
